in $ct$ for every unit of $x$ it covers. The edge moving right, $c\\,dt = dx$, is the same everywhere, and the cones follow it, since $t$ orients the cones outside the tube.","The dash dot line is $g^{tt} = 0$, where $k = 0$ and the surfaces $t = $ const stop being spacelike. The entry writes its Kretschmann scalar as $0/0$ on the axis, so the drawing marks no singular line here; the tube's curvature is concentrated in its thin walls."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"2a6af852e26ede20"}}]}}
